Design a scholarly outline that follows a review/survey arc: Introduction; Historical
background; Key concepts; Prior work; Current state and debates; Open problems; Synthesis;
Suggestions / future work; Conclusions; References. Map the arc onto the length budget above.

Requirements:
- Every section has a stable slug `id`, a `purpose`, `key_questions`, `target_words`,
  `source_domains` (subset of arxiv, pubmed, exa, tavily, wikipedia, web), and `depends_on`.
- `depends_on` lists section ids that must be drafted first. Keep it acyclic. Independent
  sections (empty `depends_on`) will run in parallel; Synthesis/Conclusions depend on the rest.
- Subsections are optional structural detail inside a section.
- Include a References section with target_words 0.
